cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software, or the derived figures and tables it publishes,
  please cite it as below. Please also cite the data sources in `references`.
type: software
title: "Starlink Differential Drag Atlas"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible pipeline and analysis testing whether Starlink hardware
  generations (v1.0, v1.5, v2-mini, v2-mini DTC, and v2-mini-opt) show
  distinguishable orbital-decay sensitivity to the same space-weather forcing
  over Solar Cycle 25, 2020-2026. Storm responses are measured against each
  satellite's own pre-storm baseline, within altitude shells, excluding
  orbit-raising, with storm-level bootstrap confidence intervals. Raw
  Space-Track data is not redistributed; derived aggregates and all code are.
authors:
  - given-names: Aviral
    family-names: Shrivastava
repository-code: "https://github.com/aviral-shrivastava-dev/heliodrag"
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
keywords:
  - Starlink
  - satellite drag
  - thermosphere
  - geomagnetic storms
  - space weather
  - Solar Cycle 25
  - superposed epoch analysis
  - data engineering
references:
  - type: data
    title: "General perturbations element sets (GP and GP history)"
    authors:
      - name: "United States Space Force, 18th and 19th Space Defense Squadrons"
    url: "https://www.space-track.org"
    notes: >-
      Accessed through Space-Track.org under its user agreement. Not
      redistributed by this project.
  - type: data
    title: "OMNI 2 hourly merged data (OMNI2_H0_MRG1HR)"
    authors:
      - family-names: King
        given-names: Joseph H.
      - family-names: Papitashvili
        given-names: Natalia E.
    url: "https://omniweb.gsfc.nasa.gov/"
    notes: "Retrieved through the NASA SPDF HAPI server. Public domain."
  - type: data
    title: "General Catalog of Artificial Space Objects (GCAT)"
    authors:
      - family-names: McDowell
        given-names: Jonathan C.
    url: "https://planet4589.org/space/gcat/"
    notes: "Source of the hardware-generation labels. CC-BY."
  - type: data
    title: "Space Weather Prediction Center real-time products"
    authors:
      - name: "NOAA Space Weather Prediction Center"
    url: "https://www.swpc.noaa.gov/"
    notes: "Used only by the optional live nowcast, not by the analysis. Public domain."
